# Cloudflare Pages reads this at the edge. Path-only matching: a rule whose
# source is a full URL is parsed and silently ignored, which is why the
# www->apex redirect is a zone-level Redirect Rule in the dashboard instead.
#
# /get IS NOT HERE ANY MORE — it is `functions/get.ts`, and that is the point.
#
# It used to be `/get  /download  301`, a blanket forward that could not do the
# one thing a short link is for: send a person to the store for the phone they
# are actually holding. Platform is a request HEADER, and path-only matching
# cannot see it, so every Android visitor — the only ones who can install the
# app today — had to read a page and find a button to reach a store they were
# already heading for.
#
# A Function does win over a matching rule here (verified against
# `wrangler pages dev`, for both /get and /get/), so this file could have kept
# a dead rule without breaking anything. It does not, because two owners of one
# path is a thing the next person would have to test to understand.
#
# WHAT WAS ACTUALLY LIVE, checked rather than assumed: nothing. The rule was
# committed in 4964d7b and never deployed, so https://cirrusquit.com/get has
# been answering 404 for as long as four published posts have pointed their
# promo card at it. The card has been dead on arrival for every reader who
# tapped it.
#
# That is worth knowing for two reasons. It is why this change is a fix and not
# only an improvement — and it means no 301 was ever served, so there are no
# permanently-cached redirects in anyone's browser to work around. The
# destination is whatever we deploy next.
